[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Installing netavark does not change your active Podman setup: CNI remains
the default in Podman 5 and continues to work as before. Podman 6 removes
the CNI backend (rejecting network_backend = "cni") and uses netavark
exclusively.

netavark is opt-in on Podman 5. Opting in gives containers name
resolution via aardvark-dns, isolated custom networks, and automatic pf
anchors, and prepares existing images, containers, and custom CNI
networks to open and run directly under Podman 6. To check readiness,
prepare the host side alone (pf anchors, sysctls, loader, dns_bind_port),
or migrate an existing CNI host, run:

  # /usr/local/sbin/netavark-migrate check
  # /usr/local/sbin/netavark-migrate host
  # /usr/local/sbin/netavark-migrate

Or opt in manually after configuring pf below by creating
/usr/local/etc/containers/containers.conf.d/50-netavark.conf:

  [network]
  network_backend = "netavark"

To switch back to CNI, run `/usr/local/sbin/netavark-migrate back` (or
remove that file and restore your CNI conflists and containers).

netavark keeps its pf rules in anchors under "netavark/". pf must be
enabled, and /etc/pf.conf must include the anchors:

  nat-anchor "netavark/*"
  rdr-anchor "netavark/*"
  anchor "netavark/*"

Existing table <netavark-subnets> and table <netavark-isolated> lines
are harmless if still present in /etc/pf.conf, though no longer needed.

To reach published ports through the host's own addresses, including
127.0.0.1, set this before pf is enabled:

  # sysctl net.pf.filter_local=1
  # echo net.pf.filter_local=1 >> /etc/sysctl.conf
  # sysrc -f /boot/loader.conf pf_load=YES

pf_load makes the setting apply at boot: sysctl.conf is read before
the pf module would otherwise be loaded.

If a host resolver binds *:53 (dnsmasq, unbound), aardvark-dns cannot
bind and podman reports "aardvark-dns failed to start". Set dns_bind_port
under [network] in containers.conf before starting containers so pf
redirects each gateway's port 53 (if changed while containers run, stop
aardvark-dns and restart containers that use DNS):

  [network]
  dns_bind_port = 5300

aardvark-dns 2.1.0 needs inotify (vfs.inotify.max_user_instances 0 or
higher, default 256).

Rules and isolation tables live inside "netavark/*" sub-anchors and
survive "service pf reload" and "service pf restart". After a bare
"pfctl -F all", reload /etc/pf.conf; if the sub-anchors themselves are
flushed, restore the rules of running containers with:

  /usr/local/libexec/podman/netavark firewall-reload

See netavark-pf(7).
EOM
}
]
